1052 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Gameplay\072\n1\056 Player spawn in the center of the bottom left room\056 \n2\056 After exploring they should note the following\072\n     \055 A red door blocked by a shelf\056\n     \055 A canon tied to a pole\056 Interacting with this should give a line \n        saying \042If this line isn\047t here\054 the canon would just slide down \n        this tilted boat\042\n     \055 A broken door\056 Interacting will say \042If only I have something \n        heavy to break this door\056\n     \055 Shelves with one containing a scissors\n3\056 Player should then use the scissors to cut the rope on the \n     cannon and the cannon will slide down to the broken door \n     smashing it open\056\n     In doing so\054 the boat will tilt even more\056 This will cause the shelf \n     blocking the red door to slide down as well\056\n4\056 Player now has access to the bottom right room\056\n5\056 After Exploring they will find a red key in the shelf in that room\056\n6\056 Player will use that key to open the red door\056\n7\056 After passing the red door\054 the player should notice that the\n    chandelier relative to the ceiling is tilted to the right of the boat and\n    swinging slightly due to the shift in weight distribution just now\056\n8\056 Exploring the large center room should give the following\072\n     \055 A empty key shelf on the bottom left that should contain the \n        Light Blue Key\n     \055 The Light Blue key behind bars which contains 5 Barrels\056\n     \055 Interact with the purple door to note that it is jammed and \n        cannot be opened\056\n     \055 Interact with barrels and note that they can pull or push the 6 \n        barrels in the center room\056\n9\056 Player should then note that their previous action with the barrel\n     caused the boat to tilt so they can try and move the barrels to the \n     left to make the boat tilt the other way\056\n10\056 After doing so the boat should tilt to the left\054 and the Light Blue \n       Key should then be slid out of room of barrels behind bars\056\n11\056 Using that key they can open the Light Blue Door\056\n12\056 They will see the escape boat but interacting with it will tell the \n       player they need to find the oars\056\n13\056 Exploring more\054 player will see a ladder\056\n14\056 Interacting with the ladder they will be prompted to either carry\n       the ladder or climb the ladder\056\n15\056 After entering the upper storage area\054 they will see the oars\056\n16\056 \050Optional\051 If they are sharp they might see that across the \n       broken wall\054 on the other side of the boat there is treasure\056\n\nWithout the treasure\072\n17a\056 They can just go to the escape boat and leave\056\n\nGetting the treasure\072\n17b\056 Player will go down the ladder and remember they can pick up \nthe ladder\056\n18\056 Player pick up ladder and move towards the high broken wall of \n       the right upper storage area with the treasure\056\n19\056 Player put down the ladder and climb the ladder\056\n20\056 Interacting with the treasure will add the treasure to inventory\056\n21\056 Player can now escape with the treasure and board the escape\n       boat\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 1051 0 R
     /Pg 998 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

